{"seq":2,"slug":"theodore-roosevelt-rise","title":"西奥多·罗斯福：崛起之路","stage":"DONE","category":"theodore-roosevelt","categoryLabel":"西奥多·罗斯福","chapterCount":3,"docCount":8,"url":"/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-rise","rating":{"composite":3.56,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":2.5,"positioning":null,"strategic":5},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"hubDir":"/Users/wangyang.learnwy/learnwy/learnwy/l-doc-hub/hubs/leaders/10_theodore-roosevelt/2_theodore-roosevelt-rise","introMarkdown":"# 西奥多·罗斯福：崛起之路\n\n1901 年 9 月 14 日，麦金莱总统遇刺身亡，时年 42 岁的西奥多·罗斯福（Theodore Roosevelt，1858–1919）在布法罗仓促宣誓就职，成为美国历史上最年轻的总统。然而，把他推上权力顶峰的并非偶然的子弹，而是此前四十余年里一条曲折而清晰的上升轨迹。这个知识库聚焦的正是这条\"崛起之路\"——从纽约曼哈顿一栋褐石宅邸里那个气喘吁吁的病弱男孩，到圣胡安山下高举马刀的志愿骑兵团中校，再到入主白宫前夜的纽约州州长与副总统。\n\n罗斯福的成长史很难用单一标签概括。他出身于荷兰裔的纽约望族，享有镀金时代上流社会的全部特权；但他童年的主旋律却是哮喘、虚弱与对自身身体的持久搏斗。父亲老西奥多对他说的那句\"你有头脑，却没有强健的身体\"，成为他终生奉行\"奋斗人生\"（the strenuous life）信条的起点。哈佛四年里，他既是博物学爱好者，又写出了至今仍被海军学界引用的《1812 年海战史》。\n\n他的政治生涯起步同样不循常规。1881 年，23 岁的他作为共和党人当选纽约州议会议员，成为当时最年轻的议员，并迅速以\"旋风般\"的反腐姿态搅动奥尔巴尼的政治格局。1884 年 2 月 14 日，妻子爱丽丝与母亲米提在同一天、同一栋宅子里相继离世，这场毁灭性的双重打击把他驱向达科他荒地（the Badlands），在那里他以牧场主、猎人和县副治安官的身份重塑了自己。\n\n回到东部后，他历任联邦文官委员会委员、纽约市警察局长、海军部助理部长，每一个职位都被他用来推动改革与现代化。1898 年美西战争爆发，他辞官从军，组建\"莽骑兵\"团并一战成名；战争英雄的光环把他送上纽约州州长之位，又在 1900 年被推举为麦金莱的竞选搭档。\n\n本知识库分为三章，沿时间轴梳理罗斯福从 1858 到 1901 年的崛起历程，力求以可核查的日期、地点、人物与原始文献，呈现一个立体、可信而非神话化的青年罗斯福。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"early-life-and-formation","title":"早年与塑造（1858–1880）","docCount":3,"url":"/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-rise/early-life-and-formation","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"gilded-age-origins","title":"镀金时代的家世与出身","url":"/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-rise/early-life-and-formation/gilded-age-origins"},{"seq":2,"slug":"asthma-and-the-strenuous-body","title":"哮喘与\"奋斗人生\"的身体哲学","url":"/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-rise/early-life-and-formation/asthma-and-the-strenuous-body"},{"seq":3,"slug":"harvard-and-intellectual-awakening","title":"哈佛岁月与智识觉醒","url":"/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-rise/early-life-and-formation/harvard-and-intellectual-awakening"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"first-steps-and-the-west","title":"政坛初啼与西部岁月（1881–1888）","docCount":2,"url":"/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-rise/first-steps-and-the-west","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"the-cyclone-assemblyman","title":"旋风议员：奥尔巴尼的初啼（1881–1884）","url":"/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-rise/first-steps-and-the-west/the-cyclone-assemblyman"},{"seq":2,"slug":"double-tragedy-and-the-badlands","title":"双重悲剧与达科他荒地（1884–1888）","url":"/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-rise/first-steps-and-the-west/double-tragedy-and-the-badlands"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"the-road-to-the-white-house","title":"通向白宫之路（1889–1901）","docCount":3,"url":"/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-rise/the-road-to-the-white-house","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"reformer-in-office","title":"改革者在任：文官与警务（1889–1897）","url":"/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-rise/the-road-to-the-white-house/reformer-in-office"},{"seq":2,"slug":"navy-and-the-rough-riders","title":"海军部与莽骑兵（1897–1898）","url":"/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-rise/the-road-to-the-white-house/navy-and-the-rough-riders"},{"seq":3,"slug":"governor-vice-president-president","title":"州长、副总统与继任总统（1898–1901）","url":"/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-rise/the-road-to-the-white-house/governor-vice-president-president"}]}]}